d_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/json","state":"uploaded","size":653,"digest":"sha256:171c173a90f62b004855a068aa8159ae2851f1c5668d1c6dd008356a2f4606b9","download_count":0,"created_at":"2026-11-19T11:51:45Z","updated_at":"2026-11-19T11:51:45Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/releases/download/m141-v0.14.1/m14stage1-starter-manifest.json"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enginsoysal/engacer-os/tarball/m141-v0.14.1","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enginsoysal/engacer-os/zipball/m141-v0.14.1","body":"# Engacer OS M14.1 / 0.14.1 - Windows x64 loader foundations\n\nDevelopment media qualified within **M14-STAGE1-VM-v1**. This extends original x64 image loading and DLL lifetime, retains the original 7-Zip console/MSI profile, and adds an optional verified Firefox installer download. Firefox and general Windows GUI installation/execution are not supported yet.\n\nUse the matching [prepared VMware ZIP](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/releases/download/m141-v0.14.1/EngacerOS-M14STAGE1-VMware.zip) or [ISO](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/releases/download/m141-v0.14.1/EngacerOS-M14STAGE1.iso). [Installation guide](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/a04ee8b564f3cd961645c617c98c74a79fb880ae/docs/handbook/install-m141.md), [Windows files and browser downloads](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/a04ee8b564f3cd961645c617c98c74a79fb880ae/docs/handbook/windows-m141.md), [full stage scope](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/a04ee8b564f3cd961645c617c98c74a79fb880ae/docs/milestones/m14-1.md).\n\nBuild: `23b939c5a022246412fcac648f5f4453`.\n\n- ISO SHA-256: `c812a14655798ba606767ae477370c26015745184e30f4271fb5817fa4a97b39`\n- VMware ZIP SHA-256: `7a7c0e1c9a5e60d877af84423393036adae1c77dea10e5a0f652267ce780b749`\n- [Complete SHA-256 list](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/releases/download/m141-v0.14.1/M14STAGE1-SHA256SUMS.txt)\n\nThe prepared package contains a new blank growable 20-GiB SATA disk, two CPUs, 128 MiB RAM and x64 UEFI with Secure Boot disabled. Extract the whole package, open EngacerOS.vmx, choose I Copied It if asked and follow setup. Installation erases the selected disposable disk. The matching ISO may remain connected after installation.\n\nThe exact candidate passes ordinary, compact and physical 4K installation and independent starts; the enabled-device VMware package passes actual installation and two disk-only starts. The original 7-Zip lifecycle verifies 106 original payload hashes. Selected original Notepad++ and SumatraPDF images are mapped/inspected without execution. Twenty sparse-image/DLL runs retain zero managed pages and peak at 134 owned physical pages; separate actual protection faults are contained. The real Firefox download is cancelled safely, then downloaded completely and independently hash-checked. These are scoped native/fixture results, not general Windows GUI or browser compatibility. [Acceptance evidence](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/a04ee8b564f3cd961645c617c98c74a79fb880ae/evidence/M14/1/acceptance-results.json), [resource limits](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/a04ee8b564f3cd961645c617c98c74a79fb880ae/evidence/M14/1/resources.json).\n\nThe 4K font-generation admission error found during development is corrected; a compile-time guard now requires the complete semantic font table. Fixed desktop state remains 557,516 bytes and font coverage remains 251,248 bytes. Historical evidence and earlier releases remain unchanged.\n\nStatic TLS, process/thread/exception expansion, normal process-detach callbacks, original Windows GUI controls and reusable MSI behavior remain later M14 stages. x86 is M15 and Win16/DOS is M16. No new long-duration stability or faster-than-Windows claim is made. M14.15 is the mandatory whole-system CPU/RAM/storage optimization gate. Read the [ordered plan](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/a04ee8b564f3cd961645c617c98c74a79fb880ae/docs/milestones/m14.md).\n"}